Smiler is a centaur who keeps [[Org/The Undertable/index|The Undertable]], a pawn shop in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Star 12/index|Star 12]]. He stands about nine feet tall and stoops under the shop's low ceiling. Bands of yellowish metal ring both his arms, gems are braided into his long beard and into his tail, and the gauges in his ears are set with stones.

Smiler sells firearms alongside the rest of his stock. He has dealt with the party before and greets them warmly, keeps a friend's discount for those they vouch for, and does not trouble himself over a buyer's age. He also passes word along, and a message left with him was meant for a man named Donnie.

He drew nine hundred gold from [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]]'s bank card and kept fifty as his fee.

He keeps a friend's discount, which the pharmacy [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Ye Olde Apothecary|Ye Olde Apothecary]] does not honor.

After the Party ended the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]], Johnny kicked in his door to announce that he had won the gang war and asked Smiler to fence the two cars they had taken from the gang's shop. Smiler said it was not his usual trade, but agreed to put out feelers. He could almost certainly find a buyer for the minivan. He would not touch the luxury Aventine, which draws too much attention; he offered instead to find someone who could swap its plates and give it a legal registration. He would not keep the cars at the shop, so the Party drove them away again. A few days later he sent a fax to the Party at the [[Sin and Tonic]] with a buyer for the minivan and an address in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]] to drop it off that night.
